From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:41:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: geometry shaders and fillModeNonSolid

KosmicKrisp already emulates tessellation with poly, the library
honeykrisp uses for geometry and tessellation on Apple GPUs, and its
pipelines already reserve a third pre-render stage. Finish the geometry
stage the same way honeykrisp does:

- The stage before the geometry shader (vertex, or tess eval with
  tessellation) runs as compute and writes its outputs to memory
  (poly_nir_lower_vs_before_gs).
- poly_nir_lower_gs splits the geometry shader into the geometry shader
  proper, run as compute once per input primitive and instance, and a
  rasterization shader, which becomes the render pipeline's vertex
  function and reads back the vertex the draw names. Its count and
  pre-GS programs are only for transform feedback and statistics
  queries, which KosmicKrisp does not expose, so they are not built.
- At draw time kk_launch_gs uploads the geometry parameters, runs both
  compute stages (for an indirect draw, sized on the GPU by a new
  libkk_gs_setup_indirect kernel and dispatched with
  dispatchThreadsWithIndirectBuffer, whose argument layout is poly's
  "indirect local" grid) and draws the rasterization shader with the
  shape poly chose: a dynamic index buffer, a static one (widened to
  32-bit, as Metal has no 8-bit indices), or none.
- Input assembly happens in software, so only primitive restart is
  unrolled before a geometry shader; the provoking vertex, the
  geometry shader's gl_PrimitiveID in the fragment shader, clip and
  cull distances and output-topology culling follow.
- A points geometry shader with a dynamic index buffer kills the ~0
  padding vertices: Metal restarts strips on ~0 but draws it in a point
  list.
- Geometry shaders unroll loops so poly can count vertices statically.

fillModeNonSolid: VK_POLYGON_MODE_LINE is Metal's triangle fill mode.
Metal has no point fill mode, so a pipeline with VK_POLYGON_MODE_POINT
gets a geometry shader of its own that emits each triangle's vertices
as points after culling the triangle as the rasterizer would (facing
from the NDC area, the viewport's y direction, front face and cull
mode, passed per draw).

DXVK requires both geometryShader and fillModeNonSolid.

Checked on the workstation only: the driver built for Linux on a mock
Metal bridge compiles and records draws for vertex+geometry,
tessellation+geometry and point/line fill pipelines, with every MSL
library fully translated. Not run on a GPU.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-kosmickrisp-gs-fill-host.md
Offered-upstream: no
