+/* poly pads each input primitive's run of a dynamic index buffer with ~0,
+ * relying on primitive restart. Metal restarts strips on ~0 but draws it as
+ * a vertex in a point list, so the rasterization shader of a points geometry
+ * shader would compute its output from vertex ID 0xffffffff, reading far out
+ * of bounds. Such a vertex computes vertex 0 instead and is killed with a NaN
